WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.990
Your heart is shouting,

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.910
"Be strong and sad!"

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.780
Just a little more, just a little bit more.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.300
Raise your hands!

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.180
I'm sure you won't realize it,

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.110
But you're the same as you always were.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.840
You smiled at me.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.940
Like a leaf swaying in the wind,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:48.790
It seems like my heart is going to explode.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.630
Your heart is shouting,

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.580
"Be strong and be sad!"

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.560
Just a little more, just a little bit more.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.480
Raise your hands!

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.250
Someday, you will be gentle,

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.350
And understand what I am saying to you!

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.210
It'll be all right, no matter where you go,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.720
This excitement will never stop!

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.370
Cannon at full power!

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.840
Let's end this year with a bang!

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.840
Hold it!

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.050
New Year's Eve. 108 Shots!

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.590
Director-san! You've got the wrong idea!

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.800
Okay! Start the countdown!

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.100
Mina-chan.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.770
Yayoi Mina
It's me, Mina.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.770
Are you alone on New Year's Day?
Do you need food?

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.770
Reply          Display     Sub-menu

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.480
Yayoi Mina
Re: It's me, Mina.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.480
Well, I'll manage. I'll be fine.
I hope you have a Happy New Year.
Riku.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.070
For now, I guess I should have some Toshi-koshi soba.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.070
TL note: "Toshi-koshi" means "New Year's Eve," and "Toshi-koshi soba" is a traditional noodle dish eaten around New Year's.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.660
Bean Curd Soba

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:20.780
Tastes great!

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:29.750
Even so, my parents have their own plans for New Year's.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.330
But it's already New Year's Day.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:34.130
Happy New Year!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:44.010
An Exciting New Year

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.040
It's already past noon.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.170
I overslept.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.170
Card says: Let's stay good friends this year! Yayoi Mina.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.090
Card says: Happy New Year. Let's do our best this year too! New Year is upon us! Watatake Haruka.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.720
Card says: Happy New Year! I wish you all health and happiness for 2007. Let's be friends this year too!! Suzuki Itta.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.470
Card says: Love from a beautiful sports girl. Kuwayama.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.850
Card says: Amamiya is Life! Doujima.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.850
Card back says: Youzou City, Tsumugino Town, 1-23-6, Aoba Riku-sama.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.690
It's from Amamiya-san!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.360
Card says: Happy New Year. Let's stay good friends this year! Wild Boar.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.700
Huh? Oh yeah. I didn't get one from Kasuga-san.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.170
Who could that be on New Year's Day?

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.560
Aoba

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.860
Th-This is his house, isn't it?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.870
Aoba

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:33.290
Aoba-kun said that his parents would be away for New Year's.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.290
It might be tough for him on his own.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.780
COMING!

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:10.740
Amamiya-san?

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.580
U-Um...

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:18.880
I heard that you'd be alone for New Year's, and I thought you might need some help.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.090
Um... Well...

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.800
Um... Is this a bad time?

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.010
No, it's not, but...

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:30.050
Um... A-Anyway, why don't you come in?

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:31.470
Okay.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:37.210
Hmmp! Just the usual New Year's greeting between friends.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:39.650
I wonder when my problems will disappear.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.110
These times makes me remember those days, even though I don't show it, I still remember them very clearly.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.400
Reaching for strength...

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:13.600
Um...

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.930
Well...

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:26.860
Oh, I know!

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:27.950
Let's watch TV!

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:32.740
The yearly special with Reina Geimi-san might be on now.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.790
Oh! We have a guest!

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.460
Card says: Happy 2007!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.880
Hey! Sorry about this, Riku-kun.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.510
My New Year's cards took longer than expected, so I thought I'd deliver this in person.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:53.800
I-I see.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.930
Hey, hey. Can I come in?

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.930
I'd like to see what your house is like.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.310
Okay...

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.610
N-No way.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:15.990
I can't believe that we hung out together since yesterday morning.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:22.290
This will get me through another six months!

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.090
Amidst the pain...

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:28.420
Idiot!

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:32.440
My heart is screaming...

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.150
Um...

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.530
Aren't you hungry?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.120
I brought these just for you, so...

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.830
Should I cook something?

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.540
Oh? You brought some groceries with you!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.290
How thoughtful of you!

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:08.670
He sent me a message yesterday saying that he'd be on his own, so I...

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.760
What's your problem?

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:14.220
You could've sent me a message too!

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.100
But...

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.310
Okay! Let's do it!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.020
Okay.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.350
Hey. Why don't you help us, Amamiya-san?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.730
A-All right.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:26.980
Sounds good.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.940
I'm so sorry.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.700
I've got no choice.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.030
Forgive me!

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.070
Mina-chan.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.070
How are things on your end?

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.280
Geez. Aren't you done yet?

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:40.330
Um...

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.370
I've never prepared fish before.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.370
And...

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.790
Want me to do it?

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:46.750
B-But...

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.840
I have to do this for Riku-san today...

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:49.960
Okay, okay.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.090
Give me that knife.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.060
Kasuga-san...

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.770
What's wrong, Yayoi-san?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.360
Oh, it's nothing.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.030
I see.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.070
I've got to do my best too!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.280
No Boys in the Kitchen!!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.790
It's too quiet in there. I'm scared.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.220
H-How did you make all this?

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.560
Isn't it great, Amamiya-san?

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.430
I never expected to make so much food so quickly!

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.850
I'm just used to cooking.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.320
And besides, your dishes are simply splendid, Yayoi-san.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.280
You're flattering me...

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:55.610
It's really good!

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.320
I've never had anything like this before!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.490
And there are rice cakes in here!

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.990
Yeah. We usually eat it like that at home.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.660
Is that so?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.330
At my house, we bake our rice cakes and put them in our soup.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.790
Oh! That's quite different from what we do.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.000
Um...

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.590
What's wrong, Riku-kun?

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:15.760
Eat up.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.220
Y-Yeah, good idea.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.050
Your hamburger's good, Kasuga-san.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.760
Yes. What's in them?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.060
They have an interesting texture.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.390
Well, I learned it straight from Harinui-sensei.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.650
Anyway, it's a secret recipe.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:30.940
Don't say that.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.310
Please tell us.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:35.690
It's peaceful, for now.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:36.740
Thank goodness.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.780
Tokimeki. Memorial. Only Love.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:47.210
Tokimeki Memorial - Only Love. Try and say it!

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.080
There! Take that!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.090
Get ready, Mina-chan!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.300
Hojiku Taihou!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.300
TL note: "Hojiku Taihou" means "Underground Cannons."

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.390
All right!

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.810
Now I've won five times in a row!

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.190
Five in a row!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.770
Five in a row!

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.020
Okay. It's your turn now, Amamiya-san.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.440
Huh? Me?

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:23.700
Well, Mina-chan and Riku-kun are too weak. They're no match for me.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.280
Okay?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.870
But I've never played any games before.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.000
Don't worry about it!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:31.870
Here. Hold this.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.080
All right.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.300
Okay. Here we go.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.760
Start!

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:48.850
Take this!

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.520
There! There!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:52.600
There!

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:55.650
There!

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.110
She's good.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.570
There! There! There!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.120
Well, I guess I really don't understand this game.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.630
All right! Let's have another match, Riku-kun!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:19.170
But... it'd be more fun if we all played something together.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.800
Just one more game!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.010
That's all, okay?

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.010
Then why don't you play her, Mina-chan?

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.760
I'll bring a game from my room.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.510
Well then, should I bring the game?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:30.890
But...

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.150
But only if you don't mind.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:39.360
No, I don't mind.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:40.900
Your room's upstairs?

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.570
Yeah. It's the first door you'll come to.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.450
The game is on the desk.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:47.820
Okay.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.330
All right! I challenge you, Riku-kun!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.120
All right.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.640
Is this his room?

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.970
This is Aoba-kun's room.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.130
Zombies

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:43.110
His mobile... phone.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:48.490
He sent me a message yesterday saying that he'd be on his own, so I...

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.910
What's your problem?

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:54.530
You could've sent me a message too!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.120
But...

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.080
A message?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:00.120
If I...

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:03.500
If I wasn't so stubborn back then,

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.750
he would've sent me a message as well.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.760
AMAMIYA-SAN!

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.720
What's the big holdup, Amamiya-san?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.760
Oh, this must be Riku-san's room.

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:16.520
Sorry about this, Amamiya-san.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.310
I made you do all this for me.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.480
I-It's nothing.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.810
Oh! Riku-kun's room is so neat and tidy!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:26.730
Yes. It's even tidier than my room.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.450
Hey. Don't stare like that.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.450
Now then.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:37.040
I wonder what secrets Riku-kun's hiding in his closet!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.410
Hey! Don't open that!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.050
Hey. What's all this?

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:52.220
Well, cleaning up is such a bother, so I shoved everything I don't use into my closet.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.140
Geez.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.470
Oh, this...

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:04.380
Just a little more, just a little bit more.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.690
Whoa! Take a look at this!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:12.150
It says that the one I've longed for is close by!

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:16.450
Wow. So if you can find a lover, you won't have to worry about anything.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.330
Don't believe that rubbish.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.500
Humans always want to believe in something at New Year's.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.460
I agree.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:26.880
There are times when we need our dreams to live, after all.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.380
You've always got a lot to say.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:32.880
You think so?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:36.470
Oh! I'm feeling good today, so it's my treat!

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:37.470
Let's go have a drink!

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.180
Okay?

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.730
Th-This can't be true!

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.610
Paper says: Terrible Luck. The one you are longing for will not come.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:55.570
I've waited so long for this...

00:16:58.830 --> 00:16:59.160
There!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.080
Here!

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:19.140
I guess I can't compete against someone who trains every day.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.430
You flatter me.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.480
Okay! It's my turn now!

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:28.690
So, here we go, Mina-chan.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.070
Okay.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:30.730
There!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.070
Aoba-kun.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.250
A-Amamiya-san.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.460
I'm so sorry.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.790
I shouldn't have left the dishes like this.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.170
Oh, not at all.

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:53.090
I said I'd clean this up.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:04.680
Was I... a nuisance?

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.600
What? Of course not!

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:10.400
But I just barged in here all of a sudden.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.980
Well, it was a surprise, but...

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:16.320
I didn't expect everyone to get along so well.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.740
But it's much better than being alone.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:25.790
Thank you, Amamiya-san.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.330
Aoba-kun.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.270
Um... Aoba-kun...

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.100
I...

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.280
Um... Well...

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.620
Oh, I see.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:07.250
Then, we can't afford to lose!

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.330
R-Right.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.460
Huh? What do you mean?

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.420
We've gotta have a Cleaning Up Contest now!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.630
WHAT?! Why?

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:22.270
To my lovers side...

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:27.710
Was it just my imagination?

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.710
Treasures...

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.610
Um...

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.610
I-I'm so sorry.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:40.860
Oh, that's all right.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.780
It's no big deal.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:56.920
Since it's New Year's Day, let's go to the shrine!

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.090
Yes!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:04.090
Sign says: Offerings.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.100
Ummm...

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:20.150
I pray that we'll win the tournament, and that I'll get along better with Riku-kun...

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:25.370
I pray that I can see the dolphins, and that I can go on a date with Riku-san...

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:36.290
What's wrong, Amamiya-san?

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:38.420
I-It's nothing.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.930
Hey, Riku-kun!

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.350
Omikuji

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.140
Let's get our Omikujis!

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.140
TL note: An Omikuji is a strip of paper with a written fortune that is available at a New Year's shrine.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.020
Okay!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.520
Let's go, Amamiya-san.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:56.730
All right.

00:20:57.110 --> 00:21:05.820
Omikuji

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:01.690
Omikujis! How about an Omikuji?

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:06.200
As a special New Year's bonus, there are even more "Excellent Luck" fortunes available!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.280
Hey, Mina-chan. What did you get?

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:09.450
I got excellent luck.

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:10.330
Me too.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.620
Oh no! I got bad luck!

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.580
Oh, too bad!

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.170
How about another one?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:18.920
HEY!

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.130
Riku-kun!

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.380
Everyone!

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.680
Aoba. What've you been doing today?

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.550
Well, I...

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:28.470
Lots of stuff happened...

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:29.930
"Lots of stuff"?

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:33.980
We were looking forward to hanging out with you!

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:34.850
Hey!

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.940
You're so inconsiderate!

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.940
I'm gonna drop you off the edge!

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.520
H-H-H-Hey, wait!

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:10.880
I wish for world peace.

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.220
Achoo!

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:27.530
My heart is overflowing!

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:42.790
My heart is overflowing!Even if I try to conceal my feelings for you,

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:48.680
I can't help blushing when our eyes meet.

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.390
I kept this a secret from my friends,

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:03.820
Because I didn't want to be teased.

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:13.160
The important thing that nobody knows,

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:20.290
I'll only tell to you.

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:25.090
These gently falling flower petals

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:28.670
are sneaking into my heart.

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:35.050
I want to make your heart flutter.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:39.640
It's okay to have hopes

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:43.310
for the future we await, right?

00:23:43.650 --> 00:23:49.530
My heart is overflowing!

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:52.660
Next Episode Preview

00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:51.860
Oh, what to do?

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:54.560
Valentine's Day is almost upon us, and the whole school is really excited.

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:55.820
Oh, Miss Secretary. This is for you.

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:56.520
For me?

00:23:56.550 --> 00:23:59.170
It's some chocolate. I thought you might need some now.

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:01.040
Chocolate?

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:02.540
Amamiya-san...

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:03.790
I-I can't!

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:05.130
We're both ladies!

00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:09.130
I'd rather not wait for someone who may or may not come.

00:24:09.370 --> 00:24:11.520
Next on Tokimeki Memorial - Only Love:

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:12.980
An Exciting Present.

00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:14.010
Please watch it.

00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:16.590
Oh! Whatever shall I do?

00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:19.210
When you're tired, you really should eat something sweet.
